# Sales Data Analysis Dashboard

This notebook analyzes sales data using Pandas and generates insights.
1. Import Libraries (Code cell)
import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
2. Load Dataset
df = pd.read_csv('../data/raw/sales_data.csv')
df.head()
3. Basic Info
df.info()
df.describe()
4. Data Cleaning
df = df.drop_duplicates()

df.fillna(method='ffill', inplace=True)
5. Total Sales
total_sales = df['total_amount'].sum()
print("Total Sales:", total_sales)
6. Top Products
top_products = df.groupby('product_id')['total_amount'].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)
top_products.head()
7. Monthly Sales Trend
df['order_date'] = pd.to_datetime(df['order_date'])
df['month'] = df['order_date'].dt.to_period('M')

monthly_sales = df.groupby('month')['total_amount'].sum()
monthly_sales
8. Line Chart
monthly_sales.plot(kind='line')
plt.title("Monthly Sales Trend")
plt.show()
9. Category-wise Sales
category_sales = df.groupby('category')['total_amount'].sum()
category_sales
10. Pie Chart
category_sales.plot(kind='pie', autopct='%1.1f%%')
plt.title("Category Distribution")
plt.show()

## Key Insights

- Electronics has highest sales
- Sales peak observed in March
- Majority revenue comes from top 3 products

## Conclusion

This project demonstrates how data analysis helps in business decision making.
